    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find the value of \\(a\\) for which \\(g(a) = 0\\), we start with the function \\(g(x) = 3x - 4\\). We need to solve the equation:\n\n\\[\ng(a) = 0\n\\]\n\nSubstituting \\(g(a) = 3a - 4\\) into the equation, we get:\n\n\\[\n3a - 4 = 0\n\\]\n\nNext, we solve for \\(a\\) by isolating the variable. We do this by adding 4 to both sides of the equation:\n\n\\[\n3a - 4 + 4 = 0 + 4\n\\]\n\nThis simplifies to:\n\n\\[\n3a = 4\n\\]\n\nNow, we divide both sides by 3:\n\n\\[\na = \\frac{4}{3}\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\(a\\) that satisfies \\(g(a) = 0\\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{4}{3}}\n\\]",
